From gallatin@cs.duke.edu  Fri Jul 9 10:36:03 1999
From: Andrew Gallatin <gallatin@cs.duke.edu>
To: mts@off.to
Date: Fri, 09 Jul 1999 10:36:03 +0000
Subject: Re: poor network performance on de0's on 21164's.

Michael T. Stolarchuk writes:
 
<sees terrible performance & collisions with de cards & switch in
100/fdx mode>

 > 
 > Can someone explain to my what's wrong?
 > 
 > 
 > 
 > mts.


Maybe.  Newer dec-tulips (like the 21143), cannot be reliably put into
100-fdx mode with the current BSD driver.  I've been complaining about
this for years.

Jason Thorpe mentioned he was working on a new tulip driver.  When
that's ready, we can hope it will fix the problem.  Until then, try
putting your switches (&cards) into half-duplex mode.

Cheers,

Drew

